=== fast (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi fast [OPTIONS] [PATH]...
Syntax-only whole-project facts (no compiler)

Examples:
  ryi fast crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/type_ladder/src/_1_none.rs
  ryi fast --lines crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/type_ladder/src/_1_none.rs

Common: --entry <FILE> | --depth <N> | --root <DIR> | --lines

Flags:
  --fast-receivers <written>  Resolve written receiver types in fast mode
  --pattern <GLOB>  Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input
  --sqlite <PATH>  Write to a new SQLite database instead of stdout
stderr:
=== slow (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi slow [OPTIONS] [PATH]...
The SCIP oracle written as fast's tables

Examples:
  ryi slow --no-checker --scip-index crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship/fixture.scip crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship/animal.ts
  ryi slow --no-checker --lines --scip-index crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship/fixture.scip crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship/animal.ts

Common: --entry <FILE> | --depth <N> | --root <DIR> | --lines

Flags:
  --pattern <GLOB>  Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input
  --sqlite <PATH>  Write to a new SQLite database instead of stdout
  --scip-index <FILE>  Load this index.scip instead of finding or building one
  --scip-timeout <SECS>  Seconds allowed for one indexer run
Switches:
  --no-checker  Skip the compiler checkers
