=== scip (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi scip [OPTIONS] [PATH]...
Raw SCIP index rows

Examples:
  ryi scip --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship --scip-index crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship/fixture.scip --raw
  ryi scip --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship --scip-index crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/scip_relationship/fixture.scip --raw --records document

Common: --entry <FILE> | --depth <N> | --root <DIR> | --lines

Flags:
  --pattern <GLOB>  Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input
  --sqlite <PATH>  Write to a new SQLite database instead of stdout
  --scip-index <FILE>  Load this index.scip instead of finding or building one
  --scip-cache <DIR>  SCIP index cache directory
  --scip-timeout <SECS>  Seconds allowed for one indexer run
  --indexer <LANG>  Run only this language's SCIP indexer
  --records <KINDS>  Only these --raw record kinds (comma-separated)
Switches:
  --raw  Stream the index records themselves instead of the scip_* relations | --occurrence-text  Add the source text to each scip_occurrence
  --scip-build  Build the index for --raw with the inputs' language indexer
