=== query (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi query [OPTIONS] [PATH]...
Run a tree-sitter query over files

Examples:
  ryi query --query '(function_item name: (identifier) @name)' crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/type_ladder/src/_1_none.rs
  ryi query --lang rust --query '(struct_item name: (type_identifier) @name)' crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/type_ladder/src/_1_none.rs

Common: --entry <FILE> | --depth <N> | --root <DIR>

Flags:
  --pattern <GLOB>  Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input
  --lang <LANG>  Language name (default: from each file's extension)
  --query <QUERY>  Tree-sitter query text
  --scmpp <FILE>  scm++ query file: nested relations lowered to SQL over capture and CST rows
  --digest <DIGEST>  Expected content digest (one input only)
  --sqlite <PATH>  Write to a new SQLite database instead of stdout
  --timeout <SECS>  Seconds the scm++ run may take
stderr:
=== graph (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi graph <QUESTION> [PATH]...
Ask one question of the resolved call/type graph

Examples:
  ryi graph --callers slug --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic
  ryi graph --from boot --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic

Common: --entry <FILE> | --depth <N> | --root <DIR>
  --callers <[PATH#]NAME>  incoming calls to [PATH#]NAME | --uses <NAME>  Declarations that reference type NAME | --from <[PATH#]NAME>  reachability from [PATH#]NAME
  --call-path <[PATH#]NAME>  shortest call paths from [PATH#]NAME | --type-path <[PATH#]NAME>  shortest type paths from [PATH#]NAME

Flags:
  --fast-receivers <written>  Resolve written receiver types in fast mode
  --pattern <GLOB>  Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input
  --flow-path <BLOB@START:END>  value paths from PATH@START:END or tagged BLOB@START:END
  --slice <PATH:BYTE>  Control-dependence slice at PATH:BYTE
  --sqlite <PATH>  Keep the fact store in a new SQLite database at PATH
  --timeout <SECS>  Seconds the question may run
  --at <REV>  Query a committed revision
  --compare <REV>  Diff the answers against REV
  --scip-index <FILE>  Load this index.scip
Switches:
  --reverse  Follow incoming value-flow edges to answer what reaches the seed | --slow  Walk the SCIP oracle's edges (ryi slow) instead of the syntax resolve
  --rust-checker  Add rust-analyzer type evidence | --ts-checker  Add TypeScript checker type evidence
  --go-checker  Add go/types type evidence
