=== stratify (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi stratify [OPTIONS] [PATH]...
Rank files from entrypoints and propose dependency-first numeric prefixes

Examples:
  ryi stratify --from crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/app.ts --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic
  ryi stratify --kind call --from crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/app.ts --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic

Common: --entry <FILE> | --depth <N> | --root <DIR>

Flags:
  --pattern <GLOB>  Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input
  --from <PATH[:NAME][=RANK]>  reachability from [PATH#]NAME
  --base-lines <N>  Base line target
  --kind <KIND>  Edge plane used to build the graph (call, type, or both)
stderr:
=== rename (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi rename [OPTIONS] [TARGET] [NEW]
Rename a symbol and every occurrence bound to it

Examples:
  ryi rename crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/util.ts#slug slugged --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic
  ryi rename crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/util.ts#slug slugged --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic --text-refs

Common: --root <ROOT>

Flags:
  --list <LIST>  TSV of anchor<TAB>old<TAB>new rows
  --state <STATE>  Soopy state root, outside the corpus
  --at <AT>  Byte offset of the declaration when OLD is declared twice
  --verify-scip <INDEX>  SCIP index (default ROOT/index.scip): its seats join the plan
Switches:
  --slow  Plan with the compiler: the TypeScript 7 checker for TypeScript, rust-analyzer for Rust | --commit  Apply instead of dry run
  --text-refs  Report leftover old-name spellings in plain text | --no-scip-merge  Only report the SCIP diff
  --json  End with one JSON line of abstains
stderr:
=== move (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi move [OPTIONS] [OLD] [NEW]
Move a file and repair every specifier that names it

Examples:
  ryi move crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/util.ts crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/utils.ts --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic
  ryi move crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/util.ts crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic/src/utils.ts --root crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/cleave_ts/basic --text-refs

Common: --root <ROOT>

Flags:
  --list <LIST>  TSV of old<TAB>new rows
  --verify-cwd <VERIFY_CWD>  Directory --verify runs in (default: first root)
  --state <STATE>  Soopy state root, outside the corpus
  --verify <VERIFY>  Command to run after --commit
Switches:
  --commit  Apply instead of dry run | --shim  Leave a reexport shim at OLD instead of rewriting importers
  --relocate-mod  Move a Rust module's `mod` line instead of adding #[path] | --text-refs  Report leftover old-path spellings in plain text
