stderr:
=== flags (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi [OPTIONS] [PATH]...
       ryi <COMMAND>
Source files -> flat graph facts (JSONL on stdout, or --sqlite)

Examples:
  ryi crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/type_ladder/src/_1_none.rs
  ryi --lines crates/sprefa-extract/tests/fixtures/type_ladder/src/_1_none.rs

Common: --entry <FILE> | --depth <N> | --root <DIR> | --lines

Flags:
  --fast-receivers <written>  Resolve written receiver types in fast mode
  --pattern <GLOB>  Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input
  --kinds <KINDS>  Fact kinds per file (cst,type,call,df,data,cfg)
  --arms <ARMS>  Resolve arms under --resolve (call,type,flow)
  --sqlite <PATH>  Write to a new SQLite database instead of stdout
  --scip-index <FILE>  Load this index.scip
  --scip-timeout <SECS>  Seconds allowed for one indexer run under --scip-build
  --max-bytes <BYTES>  Skip inputs over this many bytes (0 = no limit)
Switches:
  --bench  Time extraction and print per-family counts to stderr | --resolve  Resolve cross-file edges over all given paths
  --rust-checker  Use rust-analyzer for Rust call/type targets | --ts-checker  Use the TypeScript compiler for TS call/type targets
  --go-checker  Use go/types for Go call/type targets | --scip-build  Build the index with the language's indexer, then load it
  --scip-deps  File-to-file edges folded from a SCIP index | --deps  File-to-file edges resolved from syntax, no index
  --package-deps  Manifest-to-manifest workspace edges | --file-fact  Prepend one file record: path, digest, bytes, lines
  --witness  Wrap output in the TSI envelope

Global: --format jsonl
Logging: RUST_LOG; HAFLEY_LOG_FORMAT=json|text
stderr:
